    "body": "### Why\n[kmp-lsp](https://github.com/Hessesian/kmp-lsp) is a language server for Kotlin Multiplatform projects (Kotlin, Java, and Swift). It is built on tree-sitter, so it starts without a JVM or a Gradle import. It has 193 GitHub stars, a release every month (v0.27.0 on 2026-09-24), a Mason package (`kmp-lsp`), and a VS Code extension. Kotlin users are already served here by `kotlin_language_server` and `kotlin_lsp`.\n\n### What\nAdd `lsp/kmp_lsp.lua`, so users can enable it with `vim.lsp.enable('kmp_lsp')`.\n\n### Notes\n- `.git` is the first root marker. kmp-lsp moves the client's `rootUri` up to the nearest `.git` ([`workspace_root_from_client`](https://github.com/Hessesian/kmp-lsp/blob/cd086c8fa363e442b88223ec8c23fa39ea41d609/src/backend/init.rs#L57-L62)). When build files come first, a repository with two Gradle builds starts two clients, and each server indexes the whole repository.\n- The server works on a single file with no root, so `workspace_required` is not set.\n- Tested with Nvim 0.12.5 and kmp-lsp 0.27.0 on macOS, in a KMP-shaped repository: go-to-definition across modules, hover, and one client for the Kotlin and Swift files.\n",
